1. npm init and install dependences.
2. connect to the DB , and dont forget to require("dotenv").config.

3. Create the model. Using new mongoose.Schema({}) and mongoose.model("collection name", modelName);
4. Create the routes for that.

5. then const router = express.Router()
6. while creating routes dont forget to const { body , validatonResult} = require("express-validator")

7. while writing anything is async function use try and catch block
8. When routers are created to export:  module.exports = routers;


and in index.js / app.js we do app.use(express.json()) if we are using json format. also this is where we use app.listen() to connect to the port.

*** dont forget to return res.status() for success and error very IMPORTANT. *** 